    {
      "id": "07483529e28a9ea9438473483970fbb1779d8cd2",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 528742352,
          "type": null,
          "body": "I have uploaded https://gitlab.com/wireshark/wireshark/-/merge_requests/2378\n\nIt adds a tools/commit-msg, which in turn calls validate-commit.py with a command-line arg so that it only calls verify_body().  If the check fails (and therefore would fail when called from .gitlab-ci.yml), the local commit will fail with the explanation of why.\n\nDo we want to do this?  Users would then be asked to install 2 scripts (presumably in https://www.wireshark.org/docs/wsdg_html/#ChSrcCodeRequirements).\n\nThere is a comment at the top of validate-commit.py suggesting it gets used as .git/hooks/post-commit, although presumably that would be too late to stop the commit?",
          "author": {
            "id": 6810036,
            "username": "martin.r.mathieson",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Martin Mathieson",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
