    {
      "id": "7cd40a4056e5d0bcc5b2e33bb2d2654a8f82683f",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 528770459,
          "type": null,
          "body": "I think one of the underlying issues here is that GitLab's CI supports success and failure for jobs, but doesn't have an easy way to convey warnings back to the merge requester. (To be fair, it's not alone in that regard.) It looks like we might be able to post comments to a MR from a CI job using [lab](https://github.com/zaquestion/lab)'s [mr note command](https://zaquestion.github.io/lab/lab_mr_note.html), e.g. something like\n\n    lab mr note $CI_MERGE_REQUEST_ID \\\n        -m \"Your commit subject is too long. Think of the children running `git log --oneline`!\" \\\n        -m \"You forgot to add your new routine to /debian/libwireshark0.symbols\"\n\nIf that sounds useful we can add `lab` to our Docker images.\n\n(I'd go even further and force-update the MR description to match the commit message(s) whenever they get out of sync, but I might be the only one with that particular peeve.)",
          "author": {
            "id": 860017,
            "username": "geraldcombs",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Gerald Combs",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://gitlab.com/uploads/-/system/user/avatar/860017/avatar.png?v=1789948913",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/geraldcombs"
          },
          "created_at": "2021-03-14T00:10:02.139Z",
          "updated_at": "2021-03-14T00:10:02.139Z",
